Source: rsetup-next
Section: admin
Maintainer: xzl <xiangzelong@radxa.com>
# dh_installsystemd 自 debhelper 13.11.6 起才解析 /usr/lib/systemd/system 下的单元
# （官方 changelog 条目 "Support units below /usr"，详见 debian/rules 注释与
# debian/README.source）。本源码包三个包的 unit 全部装在 /usr 下：低于该版本的 helper
# 会「没看见单元」而生成不含任何激活片段的脚本，把打包伪装成通过，所以下限绑定在构建
# 工具上，由 dpkg-checkbuilddeps 在任何构建规则运行前失败。这是构建工具版本下限，不是
# Rust 版本锁定；也不得用 dpkg-buildpackage -d 跳过依赖检查后再宣称打包通过。
Build-Depends:
 cargo,
 debhelper (>= 13.11.6~),
 debhelper-compat (= 13),
 nodejs,
 npm,
 rustc,
Standards-Version: 4.7.4.1
Rules-Requires-Root: no
Homepage: https://github.com/xzl01/rsetup-next
Vcs-Browser: https://github.com/xzl01/rsetup-next
Vcs-Git: https://github.com/xzl01/rsetup-next.git

Package: rsetup-next
Priority: optional
# 仅维护 64 位 amd64/arm64（用户既定口径）：不再使用 Architecture: any，
# 32 位架构（armel/armhf/i386 等）不在本项目支持范围内。
Architecture: amd64 arm64
Depends:
 apt,
 btrfs-progs,
 ca-certificates,
 curl (>= 7.63),
 device-tree-compiler,
 e2fsprogs,
 iproute2,
 mtd-utils,
 pkexec,
 systemd,
 xz-utils,
 ${misc:Depends},
Suggests:
 docker.io,
 ffmpeg,
 gpiod,
 network-manager,
 openssh-server,
 v4l-utils,
Description: local control center for Linux single-board computers
 rsetup-next provides one typed control plane for observing and managing a
 Linux single-board computer. It includes a scriptable command-line interface,
 an interactive terminal interface, and a loopback Web control center.
 .
 Mutating operations are dry-run by default and require explicit live execution
 and confirmation.

Package: rsetup-controller
Priority: optional
# 与 rsetup-next 同一架构口径：仅维护 64 位 amd64/arm64，不做 Architecture: any。
Architecture: amd64 arm64
Depends:
 adduser,
 ca-certificates,
 systemd,
 ${misc:Depends},
Suggests:
 mariadb-server,
 nginx,
Description: Web control center (controller) for rsetup-next
 rsetup-controller is the standalone HTTP control-plane process of rsetup-next:
 it serves the embedded web UI and its typed API from a loopback listener
 (127.0.0.1:8080 by default) on top of a MySQL/MariaDB or TiDB database. It
 terminates no TLS and is not designed for exposure to untrusted networks.
 .
 The package installs the binaries, one systemd unit and a documentation
 example configuration, and configures or enables nothing: an operator must
 create /etc/default/rsetup-controller (database URL, allowed Host list, allowed
 browser Origin, management cursor secret), bring the target database to the v4
 schema with rsetup-controller-migrate, and only then start the service. That
 tool is v4-only and offers no upgrade path: on an empty database it creates the
 full v4 baseline, on a database already at v4 it only re-runs its read-only
 verification, and any other schema version is refused.
 .
 The unit drops privileges to the static system account rsetup-controller,
 which the package creates on install (adduser --system) so that
 /var/lib/rsetup-controller keeps one stable owner across restarts.

Package: rsetup-board-agent
Priority: optional
# 与其余两个包同一架构口径：仅维护 64 位 amd64/arm64，不做 Architecture: any。
Architecture: amd64 arm64
Depends:
 systemd,
 ${misc:Depends},
Description: board-side agent for rsetup-next
 rsetup-board-agent is the agent process intended to run on a managed single
 board: it answers the controller's typed read-only queries (capabilities,
 device status, clock, durable task journal) from a local, read-only source and
 keeps a durable task journal under its own state directory.
 .
 The unit starts the production mode --connect: an active outbound TCP
 connection to the controller, a v3 client handshake verified against explicit
 controller public-key pins (no trust-on-first-use), an encrypted record layer,
 then an HTTP/2 dual-stream session carrying the read-only actions and journal
 queries. The process listens on no port. Every connection parameter, the pins
 included, is read from a required environment file this package deliberately
 does not ship, and the durable journal plus the board identity key live in a
 state directory created 0700.
 .
 The unit is installed disabled and starts nothing on its own: an operator must
 create that configuration file and enable the service by hand, and installing
 or upgrading never enables, starts, restarts or stops it. It runs as root
 because reading the board's full hardware state requires root privileges. A
 real host reboot boundary is still not implemented: the unit injects no reboot
 dispatcher, both reboot actions answer "capability unavailable", the advertised
 capability list does not claim reboot, and neither the binary nor the unit
 reboots the machine.
